# ThreatForge Output — SIGNATURES
# CVE:       CVE-2026-56191
# Product:   microsoft exchange
# Tags:      [RCE] [CRIT] [T1]
# Score:     90
# Tier:      CRITICAL — ACT NOW
# Generated: 2026-07-30T03:00:51.278049Z
# Status:    OK
# ---

# Confidence: No public PoC known — pattern inferred from the CVE/advisory
# description only. The vulnerability is described as a broken/improper
# authentication flaw in Microsoft Exchange Online permitting data tampering
# over the network (AV:N/PR:N/UI:N, CVSS 10.0 CRITICAL) [1][2]. No
# proof-of-concept code or published exploit traffic analysis is available
# at time of rule authoring.
#
# No packet-capture (PCAP) data source is available to this pipeline —
# this pattern is NOT verified against captured exploit traffic.
#
# *** ANALYST REVIEW REQUIRED BEFORE DEPLOYMENT ***
# Because Exchange Online is a Microsoft-hosted SaaS service, direct
# on-premises network inspection of server-side traffic is generally not
# feasible. This rule targets HTTP requests to Exchange-style endpoints
# that lack expected authentication headers (Authorization absent or
# empty), which is the network-observable behaviour most consistent with
# a broken/improper authentication exploit (AV:N/PR:N/UI:N) [1][3].
# The match logic is SPECULATIVE — the advisory page rendered no
# technical detail (JavaScript required) [2]. A qualified analyst MUST
# validate and refine the content/pcre matches against actual Exchange
# traffic before any production use. False-positive rate is expected to
# be HIGH without further tuning.
#
# SEVERITY DISCREPANCY NOTE: Only a single CVSS score is present in the
# provided context (CVSS 10.0 CRITICAL [1]). No secondary scoring source
# was provided; no discrepancy to surface at this time. If NVD [1] or
# MSRC [2] publish a revised or differing score, this rule metadata must
# be updated accordingly.

alert http $EXTERNAL_NET any -> $HOME_NET any (
  msg:"THREATFORGE CVE-2026-56191 Microsoft Exchange Online broken auth data tampering attempt";
  flow:established,to_server;
  http.method; content:"POST";
  http.uri; content:"/ews/"; nocase;
  pcre:"/^Authorization\s*:\s*$/Hmi";
  threshold:type both, track by_src, count 3, seconds 60;
  reference:cve,2026-56191;
  metadata:mitre_technique_id T1190, is_kev false, status experimental;
  classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9000004; rev:1; )

